    {
      "id": "ltdDOBwQdSlHNlugeZpOp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 362.37908366257346,
      "y": 1485.710595083355,
      "width": 1270.7392578125,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1054306364,
      "version": 674,
      "versionNonce": 1389134908,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789382589691,
      "created": 1789381810244,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Back-Of-The-Envelope Estimations\nUser Base & Traffic:-\n    -DAU: 5 Million candidates, 100,000 active usres.\n    -Read-to-Write Ratio: Highly read-heavy ((Approximation)50:1).\n    -Daily Applications:5M X 0.10 applicants/day X 2 applications = 1M apllicants/day.\n    -Write QPS(Peak):1M/(86,400X0.4) = 30 Writes/sec (peak = 150 ops/sec).\n    -Search& Read QPS(Peak): 50 X 150 = 7500 QPS.\nStorage Sizing (5-Year Horizon):\n    -Profile size = 4KB(metadata, normalized skill IDs, etc..)\n    -Storage for 20M registered candidates: 20M X 4KB = 80 GB.\n    -500,000 active job posting X 10KB = 5 GB.\n    -100M cumulative applications X 1KB = 100 GB.\n    -Primary OLTP storage is moderate ( < 500 GB), meaning entire active indices and hot rows fit cleanly in memory/NVMe drives.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Back-Of-The-Envelope Estimations\nUser Base & Traffic:-\n    -DAU: 5 Million candidates, 100,000 active usres.\n    -Read-to-Write Ratio: Highly read-heavy ((Approximation)50:1).\n    -Daily Applications:5M X 0.10 applicants/day X 2 applications = 1M apllicants/day.\n    -Write QPS(Peak):1M/(86,400X0.4) = 30 Writes/sec (peak = 150 ops/sec).\n    -Search& Read QPS(Peak): 50 X 150 = 7500 QPS.\nStorage Sizing (5-Year Horizon):\n    -Profile size = 4KB(metadata, normalized skill IDs, etc..)\n    -Storage for 20M registered candidates: 20M X 4KB = 80 GB.\n    -500,000 active job posting X 10KB = 5 GB.\n    -100M cumulative applications X 1KB = 100 GB.\n    -Primary OLTP storage is moderate ( < 500 GB), meaning entire active indices and hot rows fit cleanly in memory/NVMe drives.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
